Z||000000||XDrewX||10-18-2001||01:32 PM||||I understand that the 3800 bolts up to an isuzu 5 speed with out an adapter plate.<P>I wanted to know if the transmission needs to be shifted to left, or can it remain in its original location?.<P>Can the battery can stay in the factory location?<P>Does anyone have a good website with pictures showing the swap,(using a 5 speed) in various stages?.<P><BR>Thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||htexans1||10-18-2001||02:14 PM||||Welcome to my world (the 3800 V6)<BR>Do a search on yahoo for "3800 V6 into Fiero" and you will get many web pages of people who have already accomplished this. additionally, there is a group of mine on "yahoogroups" that discusses the 3800 V6 conversions. While I do not want to "take any business away from here," the group there (3800V6superchargedfieros on Yahoo)may be helpful for the 3800 V6 conversion questions you may have as many people here may not have many answers. Hopefully this helps you in your quest for answers for "3800 Fiero related stuff." Oh, Loyde Roscoe who is on this forum and is a member of "North Texas Fieros" has done this swap also. I am still working on my 3800 project and haven't developed any pics  yet.<BR>S.Williams<BR>1988 Fiero Coupe (project)||||reg||1
